    "bleachedEventDetails": "**STUDNET ENTRY FEE IS FOR WORKSHOP ONLY- NO KIT WILL BE SENT.***\n\n7-9PM AEST\n\nJoin this hands-on professional learning workshop designed for teachers. In this session, you’ll learn how to build, program, and test a Riley Rover Rescue Line robot using the micro:bit for the Riley Rover Rescue Line Division.\n\nNo prior robotics experience is required,this workshop will guide you step-by-step through:\n\nAssembling a robot using the Micro:Bit\nConnecting and using sensors for line tracking and rescue challenges\nCoding with the micro:bit to control movement, decision-making, and automation\nTroubleshooting and refining robot performance\nTranslating the experience into engaging classroom lessons and student projects\n\nWhat’s included:\nYour workshop fee includes a complete robot kit, shipped directly to you before the session so you can build and code alongside in real time.\n\nBy the end of the workshop, you’ll walk away with a fully functioning robot, practical coding skills, and ready-to-use teaching ideas to confidently implement robotics in your classroom.",
    "effectiveBannerImageURL": "https://rcjaregistration-prod-public.s3.amazonaws.com/EventBannerImages/EventBannerImage_8177ca2a-b735-44d7-a34d-16bc84ebee40.webp",
